  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-139246\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p>If a large data set is normally distributed, it should be approximately bell-shaped. </p>\n<p>Among the given options, the only bell-shaped curve is the following:</p>\n<div id=\"graphic-q-139246-e-0\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/q-139246-e-0\"></div>\n\n<p>It's important to note that other bell-shaped distributions exist. Therefore, further tests on the data are required to confirm whether the underlying distribution is normal.</p>\n<div class=\"studentAnswerHeader\">Your Answer:</div><div class=\"studentAnswer\"><img src=\"/graphics/q-139246-a-2\"> </div></div>",
